        "comments": "The assembly bAnsAns1.hap1.1 is based on 56x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Chromosomes Z and W were identified by read coverage.\n\nStructural annotation is propagated from INSDC submissions or other annotation providers and processed to follow RefSeq standards. Functional annotation is provided by RefSeq, and is derived from model organism databases, orthologous species, curation, domain architecture analysis, and submitted information.",
